@startuml
left to right direction
actor Customer
actor Shipper
actor "Warehouse staff" as Warehouse
actor Dispatcher
actor "System scheduler" as Scheduler
actor "Public viewer" as Viewer
rectangle "LeMail parcel system" {
  usecase "US-01 Create parcel" as Create
  usecase "US-02 Assign courier" as Assign
  usecase "US-03 Confirm pickup" as Pickup
  usecase "US-04 Scan / transfer hub" as Hub
  usecase "US-04 Dispatch last mile" as Dispatch
  usecase "US-05 Confirm delivery" as Deliver
  usecase "US-06 Report failure / retry" as Retry
  usecase "US-07 Return to sender" as Return
  usecase "US-08 Cancel before pickup" as Cancel
  usecase "US-09 Detect lost / open claim" as Lost
  usecase "Public tracking / realtime" as Track
  usecase "Validate transition" as Validate
  usecase "Append audit history" as Audit
}
Customer --> Create
Customer --> Cancel
Customer --> Track
Viewer --> Track
Dispatcher --> Assign
Scheduler --> Assign
Shipper --> Pickup
Warehouse --> Hub
Shipper --> Hub
Dispatcher --> Dispatch
Shipper --> Deliver
Shipper --> Retry
Scheduler --> Retry
Shipper --> Return
Scheduler --> Lost
Warehouse --> Lost
Create ..> Validate : <<include>>
Assign ..> Validate : <<include>>
Pickup ..> Validate : <<include>>
Hub ..> Validate : <<include>>
Dispatch ..> Validate : <<include>>
Deliver ..> Validate : <<include>>
Retry ..> Validate : <<include>>
Return ..> Validate : <<include>>
Cancel ..> Validate : <<include>>
Lost ..> Validate : <<include>>
Create ..> Audit : <<include>>
Assign ..> Audit : <<include>>
Pickup ..> Audit : <<include>>
Hub ..> Audit : <<include>>
Dispatch ..> Audit : <<include>>
Deliver ..> Audit : <<include>>
Retry ..> Audit : <<include>>
Return ..> Audit : <<include>>
Cancel ..> Audit : <<include>>
Lost ..> Audit : <<include>>
note right of Audit : Only when the state transition is persisted
@enduml
